# superpowers plan-execution scratch (ledgers, briefs, review packages)
.superpowers/

# Internal working notes — plans, superpowers specs and the audit screenshot
# corpus — are kept local only. Anchored so apps/docs and any libs/*/docs stay
# tracked.
#
# `docs/migrations/` is the exception and IS tracked: CLAUDE.md's migration
# index links into it from the repository root, so ignoring it made those links
# resolve only on a machine that happened to have the files. A fresh clone got
# 17 dead links describing breaking API changes — the one part of these notes a
# consumer, or a new contributor, actually needs. See #195.
#
# A negation cannot re-include a path whose *parent directory* is excluded, so
# the exclusion is written as `/docs/*` (the entries directly under docs/) plus
# a re-include of the one subtree. `/docs/` would make git skip the directory
# without ever reading this line.
/docs/*
!/docs/migrations/
